{
  "workflow": {
    "description": "Workflow C for the personal instance (issue #459): grill an idea into tickets with a manual check at every point where the owner must settle something. A run-start gate refuses the run when the repository rule or the family allowlist forbids a bound agent, and a setup gate refuses a repository whose docs/agents/setup.yaml is missing or invalid. Up to three grill rounds follow, unrolled: a round that leaves a question open pauses on a manual check for the owner's answers, then the next round runs. The settled decisions become a spec that goes through the spec review (/review-spec) and the tickets drafted from it through the ticket review (/review-tickets); both are the critique stage templates' nodes over the critique runner, each finding the orchestrator cannot settle pausing on a needs-human manual check. The run then pauses on the publication manual check, and only after the owner passes it does the publish gate create the tickets, through the pinned ticket-publish wrapper, in the tracker the repository's setup file names. No shim node has a failure edge, so a failing gate ends the run in failure.",
    "version": "0.1",
    "id": "workflow-c",
    "entry": "gate-workflow-c-start",
    "control": {
      "max_attempts": 1,
      "max_rounds": 1
